### Two people, and every later case references them. Names carry this run's token so a second
### `--test-only` measures its own rows rather than the union with the last run's.
# @name CreateAda
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
## TEST-HAS-HEADER: Location
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/people
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{runToken}} Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada-{{runToken}}@example.test"
}

### The second, so a filter over `assignee_id` has something to discriminate
# @name CreateGrace
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/people
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{runToken}} Grace Hopper",
  "email": "grace-{{runToken}}@example.test"
}

### `email` is optional. A person the team knows by name and nothing else is a real row.
# @name CreateAnonymousContributor
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/people
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "{{runToken}} Zoe Nameless" }

### `email` is UNIQUE, so a second person at the same address is refused. This is one of the two
### facets the framework cannot check before the write — only the engine knows whether a value is
### already held — so it arrives as a 409 from the database rather than a 422 from the validator.
# @name DuplicateEmail
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [409]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/people
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{runToken}} Ada Impostor",
  "email": "ada-{{runToken}}@example.test"
}

### `format: email` is checked before the write, though — that one the framework can see, and it is a
### 422 naming the field.
# @name NotAnEmail
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/people
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{runToken}} Bad Address",
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### The team as it now stands: three people, and neither refused write left a row.
# @name Team
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/people?name=like.{{runToken}}%25&order=name.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
